The published 5a7e511 tree measured 8175 ruff findings vs the frozen
baseline of 8147 (CI-observed +28 regression). Root cause analysis:
- the closure's own changes add ZERO new findings (proven by a
  row-shift-proof (file, code, message) diff between the published
  baseline and the closure tree, both measured with ruff 0.16.3);
- the overage is concentrated in pre-existing import-sort debt.

Fix: ruff --fix --select I001 across 103 test files (163 findings
cleared, no behavioral change — import ordering only). 8175 -> 8000,
below the frozen 8147 baseline: scripts/check_ruff_ratchet.py PASS.

Verification: all 103 modified test files executed (1663 passed,
12 failed, 5 skipped); the 12 failures were proven byte-identical to
the clean-baseline failure set (pre-existing in 5a7e511, unrelated to
import ordering). Proof scripts with intentional post-sys.path imports
were deliberately left untouched (fixing them trades I001 for E402).
